# Root .gitignore — added as a required pre-step before this project's first
# `git init` (docs/production-deployment-plan.md §0.2). Two specific loose
# files at the project root look like real, unreviewed credentials and must
# never be tracked, plus general env/secret patterns as a second guard on top
# of backend/.gitignore and frontend/.gitignore (which already cover their
# own .env files independently).

# Named, real files flagged during the deployment-plan audit — not opened by
# Claude Code, excluded here by exact name out of caution. Review these
# yourself before deciding whether they belong in this project directory.
/کدها و اطلاعات حساس.txt
/TURN .txt

# Env files, at any depth — but not the *.env.example templates (no real
# secrets, just placeholders, and genuinely useful to have committed so a
# real deploy knows every variable name it needs to fill in).
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example

# Common credential/key file shapes.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
